('Package the C++ model & configuration','gpt','A reproducible project defines architecture, tokenizer, training data recipe, checkpoint schema, and commands in version control. Separate model code from experiment configuration. Keep licenses and large weight distribution explicit.','\\mathrm{artifact}=\\mathrm{code}+\\mathrm{config}+\\mathrm{data\\ recipe}','A checkpoint without its vocabulary can generate IDs that map to the wrong text even if all tensor shapes load.','Create a clean build target, a tiny fixture dataset, sample config, and a documented checkpoint manifest.','A second clean directory can run the smoke example using documented commands.','A README cannot substitute for a missing runnable entry point.','What must accompany a checkpoint?','Matching tokenizer and architecture metadata','Only a screenshot of the loss','Packaging makes the model usable outside your development session.'),
('Reproduce training & validate acceleration','mlx','Your final report must show correctness and speed separately. Preserve a CPU reference and include gradient comparisons for accelerated operations. A small deterministic reproduction run is more useful than an unaffordable full rerun.','\\epsilon_{rel}=\\frac{|a-b|}{\\max(10^{-8},|a|+|b|)}','A GPU result can be faster yet unacceptable if a causal-mask bug lowers loss through target leakage.','Run CPU/GPU fixtures, checkpoint resume tests, and a clean end-to-end tiny training reproduction.','Publish tolerances, actual errors, hardware, compiler/runtime revisions, and measured speed.','Performance without numerical correctness is not a successful optimization.','What should precede a speed claim?','A correctness comparison','A larger batch screenshot','This demonstrates that the Apple Silicon path implements the same model.'),
('Publish evaluations & a model card','gpt','A model card records intended use, training data, metrics, limitations, and known failures. Keep educational text generation and practical assistant performance separate. Include the cost and quality tradeoffs of the pretrained alternative.','\\mathrm{report}=\\{\\mathrm{metrics},\\mathrm{protocol},\\mathrm{limits}\\}','A model may have lower character perplexity but worse rule translation accuracy. Those metrics answer different questions.','Write a model card with loss curves, throughput, peak memory, test counts, invalid-output rate, and at least five failures.','Every numerical claim points to a logged run and a defined measurement protocol.','Qualitative samples alone cannot substantiate task performance.','Can perplexity replace semantic rule accuracy?','No','Yes','The report communicates what the completed system can actually do.'),
('Deliver the conversational interface','mlx','A small CLI can be a complete product when it has reliable model loading, explicit context behavior, validation feedback, and predictable exit/reset controls. Display whether a response came from the scratch model or a pretrained model.','\\mathrm{request}\\to\\mathrm{model}\\to\\mathrm{validator}\\to\\mathrm{response}','A user asks “allow adults”; the CLI should request a precise boundary when the domain definition is ambiguous instead of inventing one.','Package the CLI, write usage examples, and run multi-turn, empty-input, oversized-context, and invalid-output tests.','The documented demo works from a clean checkout and communicates validation failures clearly.','An interface that always emits text is not necessarily robust.','How should ambiguous requirements be handled?','Request clarification or abstain','Invent an unstated definition','This turns the research artifacts into a usable specialized assistant.'),
('Engineering review & your next experiment','gpt','A final review explains architecture, derivations, implementation tradeoffs, experiments, failures, and next steps. Distinguish what you implemented from what a dependency supplied. Choose the next experiment based on the strongest unresolved evidence gap.','\\mathrm{next\\ experiment}=\\mathrm{hypothesis}+\\mathrm{control}+\\mathrm{metric}','If held-out negations fail, a targeted data and semantics experiment may be more informative than doubling parameter count.','Present your model and assistant with a reproducible demo. Include a component ownership map and propose one bounded follow-up experiment.','All capstone checklist items have linked evidence; limitations state actual observed failures.','Finishing the course does not imply a tiny model matches a frontier assistant.','What should guide the next experiment?','A testable hypothesis from observed failures','Parameter count alone','You can now investigate language models independently and explain the evidence.')
